# The 2 GiB guest of the browser's steps (plan part F8; ADR-0415 item 5): run
# with `--mem 2G` (`make test-keeper`, BROWSER_MEM). The room keeper sizes the
# session from the frames the kernel has: a room of 1200M, more than a 512 MiB
# guest's session (about 356 MiB) and less than this one's (about 1.4 GiB),
# is accepted, and a limit of 1800M is refused as above the session's; `top`
# shows the room's row and the session row of the guest, as the desktop's pills
# do. The line of `make run-browser`, with a disk and without a window.
! panicked
! storage failed
< Type help to begin
< \r\n~> 
> room new tab --mem 1200M --procs 64 +w /t/w\r
< tab --colour 1 --mem 1200M --procs 64 +w /t/w
< \r\n~> 
> room tab\r
< tab /t/w> 
> grants probe\r
< limits --mem 1200M --procs 64  (room tab)
< tab /t/w> 
> top\r
< ROOM
< tab
< of 1200M
< session
< tab /t/w> 
> room set tab --mem 1800M\r
< --mem 1800M: above the session's
< tab /t/w> 
> grants probe\r
< limits --mem 1200M --procs 64  (room tab)
< tab /t/w> 
> room --leave\r
< \r\n/t/w> 
> room remove tab --kill\r
< /t/w> 
> poweroff\r
